'][0],indent=1)[:2000])\nprint(k['_doc']); print(json.dumps(k['contracts'][0],indent=1))\n\"","description":"Show schema samples"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfY2ncqszDfmpEHgZh9iE","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"7c8506af-2897-45a1-807d-cad54f74778e","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:17:18.507Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
{"parentUuid":"7c8506af-2897-45a1-807d-cad54f74778e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a1a61d0d62fa7dbf3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KFpmdaVUruqvg6kzefD8fQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Engine Capability Map. Each capability is [id, name, owner-skill, maturity, contributors?]. Maturity: E=established production, M=emerging production, X=experimental research, S=speculative. Exactly one owner per capability; contributors must coordinate through the owner's contract.\n{\n \"id\": \"ARCH\",\n \"name\": \"Engine architecture, governance & agent organization\",\n \"areas\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"ARCH.REQ\",\n   \"name\": \"Requirements & configuration profiles\",\n   \"caps\": [\n    [\n     \"ARCH.REQ.game-requirements\",\n     \"Capture target game requirements (genre, scale, platforms, online model) as engine requirements\",\n     \"engine-architect\",\n     \"E\"\n    ],\n    [\n     \"ARCH.REQ.profiles\",\n     \"Engine configuration profiles & feature sets (indie 2D \\u2192 AAA open-world online)\",\n     \"engine-architect\",\n     \"E\"\n    ],\n    [\n     \"ARCH.REQ.hardware-tiers\",\n     \"Hardware tier definitions incl. server instance classes and refresh-rate classes\",\n     \"engine-architect\",\n     \"E\",\n     [\n      \"performance-architect\",\n      \"dedicated-server\"\n     ]\n    ],\n    [\n     \"ARCH.REQ.non-goals\",\n     \"Capability & non-goal register (radar non-goals)\",\n     \"engine-architect\",\n     \"E\"\n    ],\n    [\n     \"ARCH.REQ.platform-matrix\",\n     \"Supported-target matrix (OS \\u00d7 ISA \\u00d7 GPU API \\u00d7 store \\u00d7 support tier)\",\n     \"engine-architect\",\n     \"E\",\n     [\n      \"platform-architect\",\n      \"build-system-toolchains\",\n      \"ci-cd-automation\",\n      \"certification-compliance\"\n     ]\n    ]\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"ARCH.STRUCT\",\n   \"name\": \"Structure & boundaries\",\n   \"caps\": [\n    [\n     \"ARCH.STRUCT.layering\",\n     \"Layering rules & module boundaries\",\n     \"engine-architect\",\n     \"E\"\n    ],\n    [\n     \"ARCH.STRUCT.contracts\",\n     \"Contract registry between subsystem\nSkill graph (schema v1). kind: runtime | tool | process. Runtime skills ship in builds; tool skills ship only in the tools target; process skills are organizational and outside build closure. targets: build targets a runtime skill ships in. platforms: platform-specific skills only. consumes: runtime-side contract dependencies ('?' optional, '@C-Y' = consumed by the module that provides C-Y). tool_consumes: editor/cook-side dependencies (tools target only). implements: contracts this skill implements without owning (e.g. RHI backends). workstream: integration group.\n{\n \"base\": {\n  \"minimal\": \"UI-, card- or narrative-centric games without a physics world\",\n  \"min2d\": \"Small 2D games (sprite/tile renderer, 2D physics)\",\n  \"lite3d\": \"Lightweight 3D: mobile, portable, 2.5D, stylized; CPU-submitted rendering tier\",\n  \"std3d\": \"Modern 3D on PC/console (GPU-driven rendering tier)\"\n },\n \"addons\": {\n  \"openworld\": \"Large streamed worlds\",\n  \"online\": \"Networked multiplayer\",\n  \"aaa\": \"High-end AAA feature set\",\n  \"xr\": \"VR / MR\",\n  \"ugc\": \"Mods & user-generated content\",\n  \"massim\": \"Large-scale agent simulation (RTS, colony, city, crowds)\",\n  \"sandbox\": \"Voxel / buildable sandbox worlds\",\n  \"vehicles\": \"Vehicle simulation (wheeled, flight, space)\",\n  \"team-large\": \"Large production team infrastructure (multi-user, distributed builds, farms)\"\n }\n}\n{\n \"id\": \"engine-architect\",\n \"name\": \"Game Engine Chief Architect\",\n \"tier\": \"orchestrator\",\n \"parent\": null,\n \"profiles\": [\n  \"all\"\n ],\n \"purpose\": \"Owns the engine's overall architecture: requirements and configuration profiles, layering and module boundaries, the contract registry, global conventions, build/integrate/buy decisions and cross-domain arbitration. Final authority on the boundaries between skills.\",\n \"non_responsibilities\": [\n  [\n   \"Running the ADR, fitness-function and anti-legacy process\",\n   \"architecture-governance\"\n  ],\n  [\n   \"Scheduling work across agents and the ownership ledger\",\n   \"program-orchestration\"\n  ],\n  [\n   \"Architecture inside a domain (e.g. shading-path choice)\",\n   \"render-architect\"\n  ]\n ],\n \"provides\": [\n  \"C-ARCH\"\n ],\n \"consumes\": [],\n \"expertise\": [\n  \"engine architecture\",\n  \"requirements engineering\",\n  \"trade-off analysis\",\n  \"architecture views\"\n ],\n \"kind\": \"process\",\n \"targets\": [],\n \"tool_consumes\": [],\n \"implements\": [],\n \"workstream\": \"governance\"\n}\nArchitectural contracts. Skills depend on contracts, never directly on another skill's internals. layer: 0 platform, 1 foundation, 2 engine services, 3 subsystems, 4 game framework, 5 tools; 'P' = process contract (not code). 'requires' = build-level interface dependencies; must be acyclic and point to the same or a lower layer. 'universal': 'runtime' = implicitly consumed by every runtime skill; 'all' = implicitly consumed by every skill.\n{\n \"id\": \"C-PAL\",\n \"layer\": 0,\n \"owner\": \"platform-architect\",\n \"name\": \"Platform abstraction layer\",\n \"summary\": \"OS services, CPU/GPU capability discovery and device database, windowing, display & safe area, lifecycle and system events (memory pressure, thermal/power, network reachability, audio endpoint, locale, OS accessibility settings, overlay/focus, storage, page size), clocks and clock-domain correlation, processes/pipes/shared memory/dev sockets, HTTP(S)/TLS client, permissions, thread creation/affinity/QoS and main-thread dispatch. Platform code lives only in the PAL or in a registered platform backend slot.\",\n \"requires\": [\n  \"C-BASE\"\n ],\n \"conformance\": true\n}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d0af6dbe-c89d-488e-9c64-422621ed34e5","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:17:18.599Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7c8506af-2897-45a1-807d-cad54f74778e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
