{"parentUuid":"c6be93c8-2eb1-414f-9922-9770ba722a8b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a1a61d0d62fa7dbf3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L9UHBDDRnisSFbFYCrNh78","type":"tool_result","content":"C-ERR 1 runtime core-runtime-architect | Result types, assertion tiers, fatal vs recoverable, degradation rules.\nC-MATH 1 None math-simd-numerics | Vector/matrix types, precision classes, deterministic-math variants, fixed and scalable (vector-length-agnostic) SIMD kernels, convention enforcement.\nC-MEM 1 runtime memory-allocators | Allocator interface, tagging, budgets hooks, OOM behavior.\nC-INSTR 1 runtime observability-telemetry | Log/trace/metric API; zero cost when compiled out; trace format.\nC-CRASH 1 runtime crash-diagnostics | Crash context annotations, breadcrumbs, watchdog registration.\nC-BUDGET P all performance-architect | Budget numbers per hardware tier × configuration × refresh class, derived from the performance model; perf gate thresholds.\nC-WORLD 3 None world-architect | Cells, streaming sources, world data activation in budgeted, time-sliced batches with bulk registration.\nC-EDCMD 5 None editor-architect | Transactions, undo/redo, selection, tool registration.\nC-ARCH P all engine-architect | Layer rules, contract registry, configuration profiles, conventions.\nC-ADR P all architecture-governance | ADR template incl. revisit conditions; automated architectural checks.\nC-EVID P all research-evidence | Source tiers, maturity classes, claim standards.\nC-ORCH P all program-orchestration | Ownership ledger with access classes; write sets by module convention (src/<skill-id>/, tools/<skill-id>/; tests owned by the test-owning skill); shared-file protocol; contributor semantics (review + \nC-TEST P all test-architect | Required test kinds per skill, test determinism, coverage & mutation thresholds, the evidence bundle an implementer hands to S3/S4 critics, oracle independence, conformance suites owned by contract ow\nC-API P all api-lifecycle-migration | Public vs internal APIs, versioning, deprecation windows, upgraders.\nC-TRUST P all security-engineering | Untrusted inputs list, validation obligations, sandbox rules.\nC-SCALE 1 runtime runtime-scalability | Device-profile knobs, scalability cvars, budget query/report API, actuator registration and governor control signals.\nC-EDHOST 5 None editor-ui-framework | Asset-editor host, preview-scene registration, thumbnail providers, inspector customization, tool-mode registration, shared curve/timeline widgets.\nC-CERT P all certification-compliance | Register of external requirements per program (console cert, Steam Deck Verified, store review, law) each mapped to an owning capability; owners must satisfy their entries.\nC-PERF P all performance-architect | Finding format (hypothesis, capture, attribution, expected gain), routing as a change request to the owning skill, time-boxed territory loans recorded in the ledger.\nC-BENCH P all perf-benchmarking | Benchmark registration, metric schema, C-BUDGET line reference, warm-up and variance rules, required hardware tier, replay-driven runs.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7a06865e-808d-4ca9-b6a0-9e6b16cc26e6","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:20:02.486Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c6be93c8-2eb1-414f-9922-9770ba722a8b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
