{"parentUuid":"cc1b1ceb-2423-41a7-9413-f8fdfc31b7e5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a1a61d0d62fa7dbf3","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfY37dU7TfDBSe7kDRr5P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled on all 13 findings: 8 upheld and 5 overturned. `check.py` passes with 0 errors and 0 warnings, and I checked each claimed change against the data files directly.\n\n**Upheld (8):** K-COMPLETE-3, K-FUTURE-10, K-GAMEPLAY-4, K-PERF-8, K-PROD-2, K-PROD-8, K-RENDER-7, K-SYSTEMS-14. In each case the claimed changes are in the data and resolve the critic's problem. Where the builder chose a different mechanism than the critic proposed, the choice holds up technically.\n\n**Overturned (5):**\n- **K-QUALITY-6:** the builder says the conformance flag is checked, but nothing in `check.py` or `model.py` reads it. There is also still no rule that a provider change must pass the tests consumers contributed. Required: a `check.py` error for any code contract without the flag, a self-test case for it, and the gating rule added to C-TEST or C-ORCH.\n- **K-GAMEPLAY-15:** two concerns the critic listed still have no owner: localizing AI-generated text, and saving conversational memory (no `C-SAVE?`). The skill's expertise list still has no ML competence. The builder's claim that the radar rule replaces the proposed check is wrong: the radar rule checks that experimental techniques are tracked, not that they are reached only through optional contracts, so §7's claim is still unchecked.\n- **K-LEGACY-7:** keeping both submission paths in one skill is a sound choice. But geometry-pipeline's expertise is still GPU-driven only, and the rendering critic's \"no draw-call-centric\" check is still unqualified. Those were the critic's stated root cause.\n- **K-SYSTEMS-13:** `PLAT.MOB.thermal` still reads \"Thermal & power adaptivity\" under platform-mobile, so a second thermal control loop remains possible. The governor's actuator list also leaves out frame-rate cap and P/E-core placement, which the critic named.\n- **K-TOOLS-12:** the blockout tool (world-editor-viewport) has no contract through which it can call the geometry operations placed in asset-cook-processors. That breaks the framework's rule that skills depend only on contracts. `check.py` misses it because it doesn't treat contributor links as dependencies.\n\nSeveral upheld findings carry non-binding notes about skill `purpose`/`expertise` text not updated to match new capabilities (xr-runtime, spatial-transforms). The exact data change required for each overturn is in the file.\n\nOutput: `/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-1/adjudication.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8523,"cache_read_input_tokens":112870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8523,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":758,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfY37dAWJYUCcr7gpeNxk","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"19ef7001-47db-4e65-a5ab-d93dd87d94a6","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:21:42.403Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
